---
/**
 * Analytics consent notice.
 *
 * Google Analytics sets cookies, so it is not loaded at all until someone says
 * yes. The banner is hidden by default and only revealed when no choice is
 * stored yet: an inline script in BaseLayout adds `consent-pending` to <html>
 * before paint, and global.css keys off that class, so there is no flash.
 */
---

<div class="consent-banner" role="region" aria-label="Analytics consent">
  <p class="consent-title">A small note about analytics</p>
  <p class="consent-copy">
    I use Google Analytics to see which notes get read. It sets cookies. Saying no changes nothing about how
    the site works.
  </p>
  <div class="consent-actions">
    <button type="button" data-consent-accept class="btn btn-solid">Allow analytics</button>
    <button type="button" data-consent-decline class="btn btn-quiet">No thanks</button>
  </div>
</div>
